class Temp
{
    static double tempConvert(double f)
    {
        double c = 5.0 / 9.0 * (f - 32);
        return c;
    }

    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        System.out.println("Celsius = " + tempConvert(45));
    }
}
Output: Celsius = 7.222222222222222
(temp-convert is not a valid identifier because of the hyphen, so the method is named tempConvert. 5 / 9 in integers would be 0, so 5.0 / 9.0 is used.)

